The problem is that the C/N/L alignment used in nethack is NOT the same
as the C/N/L/G/E/and combinations that are in DND.  It's based much
more on the Michael Moorcock books.  In his books, lawfuls keep their
word, didn't kill you unless you were asking for it, and would often
take up "just" (but not necessary good) causes.  Neutrals really didn't
give much of a damn about any causes and chaotics typically killed
everything they got their hands on for the sheer enjoyment of it.

Notice that while chaotics really are "evil", the lawfuls really aren't
very "good" either, most would do what needed to be done (the ends
justify the means) and would hack down children in the street if they
thought it was necessary.

Take a look at the demons & devils sometime in NH.  In DND the demons
are Chaotic evil, but in NH they're just chaotic.  The devils
are lawful evil in DND, but are lawful in NH (if "lawful"="good" then
the devils should be chaotic).


